<title>UK: Britain clears Imperial's buy of Rizla.</title>
<headline>Britain clears Imperial's buy of Rizla.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The British government said on Wednesday it cleared Imperial Tobacco Group Plc's acquisition of Rizla International, a leading maker of handrolling tobacco papers.</p>
<p>The Department of Trade and Industry said it decided not to refer the merger to the Monopolies and Mergers Commission, effectively clearing the deal.</p>
<p>Imperial unveiled plans earlier this year to buy Netherlands-based Rizla for 168 million stg plus the assumption of 17 million stg of debt.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
